<para><heading level="3">GXTK 7</heading>
</para>
<para></para>
<para> </para>
<para> GXDE&apos;s Qt Quick UI plugin &amp; component library. <linebreak/>
 <ulink url="./docs/html/"><bold>Explore the docs »</bold></ulink> <linebreak/>
 <linebreak/>
 <ulink url="https://github.com/GXDE-OS/GXTK7/actions">View CI Status</ulink> <middot/> <ulink url="https://github.com/GXDE-OS/GXTK7/issues/new">Report Bug</ulink> <middot/> <ulink url="https://github.com/GXDE-OS/GXTK7/issues/new">Request Feature</ulink> </para>
<para> </para>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md0_1s1"><sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md0">
<title>About The Project</title><para><image type="html" name="screenshot.png" inline="yes">Screenshot</image>
 <image type="latex" name="screenshot.png" inline="yes">Screenshot</image>
 <image type="rtf" name="screenshot.png" inline="yes">Screenshot</image>
 <image type="docbook" name="screenshot.png" inline="yes">Screenshot</image>
 <image type="xml" name="screenshot.png" inline="yes">Screenshot</image>
</para>
<para>GXTK 7 is GXDE-OS&apos;s QtQuick UI library &amp; style plugin that mimics Deepin&apos;s DTK2Widget library. It aims to bring the apperance of DTK2Widget back to the modern Qt6 Quick applications without need of DTK2Widget-Qt6 (I also made that library but I really want to retire that) library or any Qt private libraries.</para>
<para>Currently, GXTK7 is still in early development stage.</para>
<sect3 id="index_1autotoc_md1">
<title>Built With</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Qt6 Core</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Qt6 Gui</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Qt6 Qml</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Qt6 Quick</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Qt6 QuickControls2</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect3>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md2_1s1"><sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md2">
<title>Getting Started</title><sect3 id="index_1autotoc_md3">
<title>Prerequisites</title><para>You need a C++ compiler supporting C++17 and the Qt6 development packages installed on your system.<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Qt6 (Core, Gui, Qml, Quick, QuickControls2)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CMake 3.20 or higher</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect3>
<sect3 id="index_1autotoc_md4">
<title>Installation</title><sect4 id="index_1autotoc_md5">
<title>Build Manually</title><para>First, create a build directory and build the project: <programlisting filename=".sh"><codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>mkdir<sp/>build</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>cd<sp/>build</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>cmake<sp/>..</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>make</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Then, you may run the example: <programlisting filename=".sh"><codeline><highlight class="normal">./examples/gallery/gxde_gallery</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect4>
<sect4 id="index_1autotoc_md6">
<title>Build a Debian Package</title><para>Install the build dependencies, then build the binary package from the source root: <programlisting filename=".sh"><codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>sudo<sp/>apt<sp/>build-dep<sp/>.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>dpkg-buildpackage<sp/>-us<sp/>-uc<sp/>-b</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>This produces <computeroutput>qml6-module-qtquick-controls-gxde</computeroutput>, which installs the <computeroutput>QtQuick.Controls.Gxde</computeroutput> module into the system Qt QML directory.</para>
</sect4>
<sect4 id="index_1autotoc_md7">
<title>Build an Arch Linux Package</title><para>Build and install the package from the <computeroutput>arch</computeroutput> directory of the checkout: <programlisting filename=".sh"><codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>cd<sp/>arch</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>makepkg<sp/>-si</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect4>
</sect3>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1autotoc_md8_1s1"><sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md8">
<title>Usage</title><para>Select the style by its full module name, either in C++: <programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">QQuickStyle::setStyle(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;QtQuick.Controls.Gxde&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> or through the environment: <programlisting filename=".sh"><codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>QT_QUICK_CONTROLS_STYLE=QtQuick.Controls.Gxde<sp/>./your_app</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The <computeroutput>GxdeTheme</computeroutput> singleton (<computeroutput>import QtQuick.Controls.Gxde</computeroutput>) switches between the light and dark schemes through its <computeroutput>isDark</computeroutput> property. For more, please refer to the <ulink url="./examples/gallery/">widget gallery example</ulink> and the <ulink url="./docs/">documentation</ulink>.</para>
</sect2></sect1>
